      "prompt": "A biased spinner can only land on green or yellow. The probability that it lands on green is x, and the probability that it lands on yellow is 1 - x. Landing on yellow is 3 times as likely as landing on green. The spinner is spun twice. Find the probability that at least one of the two spins lands on green.",
      "solution_steps": [
